{
  "note": "Constraint-extraction eval corpus. Anchored to DEMO_NOW = Monday 2026-08-10 (Asia/Manila): Tue=11 Wed=12 Thu=13 Fri=14 Sat=15 Sun=16, next Mon=17. Every `expected` is a partial SchedulingConstraintSet (core/constraints.ts). Labeling conventions: morning={end:12:00}, afternoon={start:12:00}, after lunch={start:13:00}; bare weekday mention → allowedDaysOfWeek (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun); explicit or resolvable date → allowedDates; 'from X onwards' → earliestDate; 'this week only' → latestDate; approximate times ('mga 8:30', 'around 3') and references to the original booking ('same time') → unresolved=true; named-doctor insistence ('lang talaga', 'only') → hard.requiredDoctorId, polite preference → soft.preferredDoctorId; unnamed 'keep my doctor' → soft.preferSameDoctor, refusal of a new doctor → hard.requireSameDoctor. Weeks run Monday-Sunday ('next week' from Mon 2026-08-10 = 2026-08-17..2026-08-23); preference-strength language ('would be best', 'works better', 'if possible', 'sana', 'ideally') → soft fields; 'skip <period>' → excludedDates for that period literally; availability remarks ('wide open') → soft. guard=true means the message must reach a human regardless of extraction (clinical content, anger). Doctor roster for labels: doc_santos = Dr. Elena Santos, doc_reyes = Dr. Marco Reyes. Starter set (65) — grow toward 150+ by adding real (anonymized) clinic phrasings per category.",
